  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "If you are experiencing stress due to discrimination at work, it is important to take steps to address the situation and ensure your safety. Here are some steps you can take:\n\n1. Document the discrimination: Keep a record of any incidents of discrimination, including dates, times, and details of the incidents. This documentation can be helpful if you need to report the discrimination to your employer or seek legal advice.\n\n2. Talk to your supervisor: If you feel comfortable doing so, talk to your supervisor about the discrimination. Explain the situation and ask for a solution. If your supervisor is not responsive, consider escalating the issue to a higher level of management or HR.\n\n3. Seek support: Consider speaking with a trusted friend, family member, or mental health professional about your experiences. They can provide support and help you process your emotions.\n\n4. Consider reporting the discrimination: If the discrimination is severe or ongoing, you may want to consider reporting it to your employer or seeking legal advice. You can also report the discrimination to the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission (EEOC) if you believe your rights have been violated.\n\n5. Take care of yourself: It is important to take care of your physical and emotional health during this time. Consider taking breaks, engaging in activities that you enjoy, and seeking support from friends, family, or a mental health professional.\n\nRemember, it is important to prioritize your safety and well-being during this time. Take steps to address the discrimination and seek support if you need it.",
